WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.300
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.534
You're in the middle of
the PGA Tour right now.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.200
You posted this photo
that made me laugh

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.901
'cause you're traveling,
obviously.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.133
So, you're on the plane,

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.868
and then you just took a picture
of this.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.234
"Clubs fell out of the luggage
cart and sat there

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.267
for a few minutes
with no one in sight.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.634
Let's just say I was freaking
out on the inside.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.200
Here we come, playoffs."

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:26.000
-I mean, talk about a nightmare.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.534
-So you knew that -- you
recognized your clubs?

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.734
-Yeah, no, you could see
right there.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.234
I was right on the window.

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:35.334
Absolute nightmare.
My heart raced.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.901
I was sweating on the plane,
everything.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:39.868
Everything was bad.
-That's a big deal.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:43.567
-Yeah. That's all -- I need that
to actually play golf.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.834
-You actually --
-So, I need my golf clubs.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:48.234
-Sorry, everyone,
I just need clubs, your clubs.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:51.267
But I wonder if there's
any other way to do it?

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.767
I mean, I used to bring guitars
when I used to do gigs,

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:58.067
and I would hopefully talk my
way into bringing it on board

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:00.601
and, like, putting it in
the closet in the front.

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:03.734
-Well, it's about -- total,
with all the shoes,

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.367
it's about 70 pounds, so...

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.000
-There was no way that's
going to happen.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.801
-[ Laughs ]
Carry-On, yeah, no.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.267
-Can you put it
under your chair?

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:15.133
No, I can't do that either.
That's wild.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.868
I just think --
It makes me laugh.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.300
Because you're trying to
zone out.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.734
You're like, "Dude, I want to be
in the zone."

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.434
Do you do anything special?

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:23.667
You're like, "Alright,
I'm playing right now.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.200
I'm in the tournament.
I can't talk to people.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.734
I can't have my clubs laying on
the tarmac."

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:30.767
-You know, for me,
it's keep everything

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:33.367
as normal as possible and just
treat it like a normal day.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:34.801
Treat it like
a normal date night.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:38.200
Treat it like a normal Friday
night, wake up, go to sleep.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.734
-You don't have a special food
or anything?

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:43.267
-Nothing particular. Why?

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.868
-I'm just saying I saw something
on the Internet I think sparked

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:50.834
a little bit of debate,
a little bit of controversy

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:53.334
if you bring it up.
-"Contrahversy"?

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:56.434
-Yeah.
That's how they say it overseas.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:57.934
That's how they say controversy,
yeah.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.400
-Got it.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.834
-You're a big fan of
breakfast foods.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:02.968
-Love breakfast.
-Yeah.

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:06.567
-Huge fan. Yeah. Love it.
Love breakfast.

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:08.000
Got to start the day off right.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.300
-Alright, so you're making --
There's video of you doing this.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.767
You're making a bowl of cereal.
-Right.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.067
-Alright.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.868
-And here's where I get involved
and I get a little --

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.501
I almost didn't talk to you
ever again.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:20.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.801
You poured your milk in first,
then the cereal.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.634
[ Audience ohs ]
There you go.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:27.200
That's the reaction.
That's the reaction I want.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.801
That's the reaction we need!

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:33.200
Collin Morikawa, what are you
talking about?!

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.100
-Jimmy, where do I start?
Where do I start?

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.968
Look, I mean, there's
a perfect ratio, right,

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:42.133
I think we all agree,
of milk to cereal.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.734
When you put --

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.100
-Talk to me, talk to me.
-When you put in milk first --

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.801
I wish we had a bowl. I mean,
that would just be perfect.

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:52.467
When you put the milk in first,
right, you pour the milk.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.167
-Yeah.
-And then put the cereal.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:57.467
-Yeah.
-The milk doesn't splash outside
the bowl.

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.801
-Oh, how aggressive are you
pouring your milk?

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.801
[ Laughter ]
You're pouring it too hard?

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:04.534
-Well, when you have a gallon of
milk, I mean, it's heavy.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.400
-Get a half gallon.
-You know, I'm an athlete,

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.501
but I'm not like a --

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:08.567
-Maybe you can't handle
a gallon of milk.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:10.467
-I'm a small guy here.
I'm trying --

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.667
-Start with those little ones
you get in grade school.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.834
-The little cartons of milk.
-A little carton of milk.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.767
You don't aggressively throw
milk around.

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:18.934
-Hear me out. Hear me out.
Hear me out.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.801
I think everyone's going to
try this.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.100
-I don't. I don't.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:26.434
-When you put the milk
and then you pour the cereal,

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.367
especially like
a Frosted Flakes,

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.400
one of my favorites.
-Okay, I do like frosted flakes.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.100
-When you put it all the way
down at bottom and it goes

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.234
all the way to the top, that is

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:36.133
the perfect ratio of
milk to cereal.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:39.000
-But why not have cereal first,
then you can really ratio

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.300
the milk and it slowly goes in

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.834
the crevasses of
the Frosted Flakes?

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:46.667
-Because it splashes out
of the --

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.133
-Questlove, are you hearing
this dude?

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.400
-Yes, I am.
-And is this insane or what?

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.934
-Yeah, it's kind of weird, man.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.601
-There's got to be one person in
here that agrees with me, right?

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.100
-Whoo!
-Yeah, there we go.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.601
-Okay, alright. That's the
people you came here with. Yeah.

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.367
[ Laughter ]
That doesn't count.

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.200
What other cereals do you have?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.100
-Oh, you know, I grew up eating
a lot of Frosted Flakes.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:10.000
Cinnamon Toast Crunch is one.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.334
-I mean, maybe if you have --
if there are flakes,

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:14.634
sometimes there's a little curve
on one of them if you are

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:18.100
aggressively pouring milk,
maybe one little dripping.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.801
That's not going to throw off
the ratio.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:23.200
-But it never happens with milk
first, then cereal.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.300
-I think you get a little
aggressive with the cereal,

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.167
and then they sparkle
everywhere, and next thing

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.834
you know, you're pouring cereal
all over the table.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.100
-So tell me, what happens
when you eat your cereal

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.467
and then you need to put
more cereal?

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.033
Your milk is already there?

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:36.701
And how good is that second bowl
of cereal?

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.968
[ Laughter ]
-Alright, now you got a point.

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:41.200
Now I'm starting to like
this idea.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.667
I think legal for
the second bowl.

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:45.834
First bowl has got to be
cereal first, then milk.

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.334
-Just try it out.
-If you want to jump back in

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:51.133
and use that cereal milk, which
I do love, I'll dive back in.

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:53.734
But sometimes I'll --
-Try it. Try it.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:56.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:58.868
-I mean, it's almost -- I want
it to get a little soggy too.

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:00.334
I don't want it to get
completely --

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:01.667
-No.
-No, just a little bit.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:02.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.267
Now the audience is turning
on me.

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:06.767
[ Rimshot ]
No, no, no, no.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:09.200
But wait, wait, wait, I'm
talking about high-grade cereal.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.367
I'm talking about Grape Nuts.

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:15.133
That's like eating rocks. That's
like eating rocks in a bowl.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.934
You got to let it soften
a little bit

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:21.300
just for the chompers.
-That's what you do.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.968
You pour the milk first,
cereal second.

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.834
Sits on the bottom.
Mix it up.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.534
-Yeah, but Grape Nuts,
it's hard to do.

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.701
Hard to do with Grape Nuts
because they're so heavy

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:30.968
and so dense, they go right
under the milk.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:34.067
You're lost. You're like,
"Help! I lost them.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.901
I'll never see them."
It's an empty bowl.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:38.400
You'll never know how many
Grape Nuts are in the milk.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.667
-I'm going to buy you a clear
bowl so you can always see.

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:43.100
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.467
There's too much --

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:50.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:52.434
Let's talk about "Full Swing."

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:55.901
Each episode follows different
pro golfers around

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:59.400
and really gets into your life
because obviously, there's much

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.100
more to the sport than
just going

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.367
and playing for the weekend.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:04.434
It's gearing up.
It's your home life.

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:06.501
How do you do it?
How do you pour your cereal?

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:07.567
Things like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.334
But it got picked up
for season two.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:10.834
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:11.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:15.234
-You're very entertaining.

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:18.200
Do you mind having the cameras
kind of invade your life,

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.434
or did you get used to it?

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:20.734
-You know, I think it's all part
of it.

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.367
It's kind of what we do.

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:24.300
You know, obviously, we have it
on the golf course

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.567
and we're pretty comfortable
with that.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:28.234
But following them around,
following us around,

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:29.767
it took a little bit of time,

00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:31.968
but when you really dive into
it, it's everything.

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:35.567
You know, and for people in the
audience and just spectators

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:38.400
that don't know much about golf,
who only know who Tiger Woods is

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.267
and golf is played on a golf
course, pretty obvious, right?

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.267
-Yeah.

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:44.367
-It's a good insight into
what we do

00:06:44.367 --> 00:06:46.367
and learning what travel is
like.

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:50.601
We're traveling for about 25, 30
weeks a year, almost 35 weeks.

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:53.200
Sunday to Sunday.
So, put that together.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.033
And we're doing it across
the world.

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:57.267
-And we get to meet your dog.
-And you get to meet our dog.

00:06:57.267 --> 00:06:59.834
I mean, he's -- Yeah, I should
have brought him out.

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:01.334
-He's here.
-He is here.

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:03.734
-But no, keep him in the room
because he barked at me.

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:06.100
-He only barked at you.
No one else.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.033
-Why, though?
-Yeah.

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:09.801
He doesn't like men.

00:07:09.801 --> 00:07:11.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.901
-Yeah.

00:07:12.901 --> 00:07:15.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.868
That's what it was?
That's what it was.

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:19.667
Yeah, he barked at me, but then
he licked me as well.

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:20.968
-Yeah, he's cute.
-He was like, "What,"

00:07:20.968 --> 00:07:22.133
like the show "What's Up?"
He's really cute.

00:07:22.133 --> 00:07:23.534
-I think he's actually gotten
more famous

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:24.667
than me off the Netflix.

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:25.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:26.868
-Is that right?
-Yeah.

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:28.434
-Everyone asking you about
the dog and stuff?

00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:30.100
-We were on the plane yesterday
and someone was like,

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.000
"Oh, I actually recognized
your dog first.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.367
And then I saw you."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.367 --> 00:07:35.968
-They go, "Yeah, we forgot
your golf clubs,

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:37.567
by the way, but we have
your dog."

00:07:37.567 --> 00:07:38.801
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:38.801 --> 00:07:41.100
Here's Collin Morikawa
in "Full Swing."

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.400
Take a look at this.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.968
-We've been at a point now
where, you know,

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:45.868
I hadn't won since
the 2021 Open.

00:07:45.868 --> 00:07:49.100
And, you know, for me, so far
in my career,

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.701
it's been a long time.

00:07:50.701 --> 00:07:52.234
Majors are career-defining.

00:07:52.234 --> 00:07:54.033
Like yeah, you want to put on
a green jacket,

00:07:54.033 --> 00:07:57.634
but at the end of the day, you
still want to win everything.

00:07:57.634 --> 00:08:01.033
And Tiger won 80-something
times.

00:08:01.033 --> 00:08:03.334
It doesn't get tiring
winning 82 times.

00:08:03.334 --> 00:08:06.968
I mean, can I say this, I want
this one more than the others?

00:08:06.968 --> 00:08:09.200
I mean, I want them all.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.300
-Yeah! I want to win it all.
-I want to win.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.133
-Collin Morikawa.

00:08:14.133 --> 00:08:17.400
Season one of "Full Swing" is
streaming now on Netflix.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.133
More "Tonight Show"
when we come back.

